        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775806651160",
            "name": "isr_summarization model"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772712567369"
          },
          "code": "ISRSUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760437924591",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760437924593_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data \n- **Title**: \n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.Title}}`\n\n- **ProblemDescription**: \n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ProblemDescription}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES.$output.items}}`\n\nEach message includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` (ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY / ORA_SVC_RESPONSE / ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE)  \n\nUse these inputs to **reconstruct the conversation flow**:  \n- Sort `Messages` in ascending order of `CreationDate`.  \n- Interpret `MessageTypeCd`:  \n  - **ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY** → Customer-reported issue or feedback  \n  - **ORA_SVC_RESPONSE** → IT Support responses or actions  \n  - **ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE** → Internal-only notes or system actions (include only if directly relevant)  \n\n---\n\n# Instructions\nReview the above `Input Data` and write a **detailed yet concise paragraph** summarizing the **interaction between IT Support and the Employee**. Highlight the **key milestones in chronological order** and the **actions taken to address any reported issues**, including both IT Support actions and Employee responses or confirmations. The summary must be written as a **single, continuous paragraph**.\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n---\n\n\n### Mandatory Guidelines  \n\n1. **Scope and Focus**  \n   - Describe only factual details from the record: the reported problem, key actions by IT Support, Employee responses, confirmations, outcomes, and any pending tasks or follow-ups.  \n   - Include references to diagnostic checks, fixes, or coordination steps only when explicitly mentioned.  \n\n2. **Role Clarity**  \n   - Refer only to “IT Support” and “Employee.” Do not include names, titles, or departments.  \n\n3. **Chronological Order**  \n   - Reorder messages based on `CreationDate` to ensure a clear timeline of events.  \n   - If timestamps are inconsistent, infer logical order (e.g., issue → investigation → solution → confirmation).  \n\n4. **Language**  \n   - Use clear, active, and professional language.  \n   - Avoid speculative or informal phrasing.  \n\n5. **Data Discipline**  \n   - Do not mention message type codes or any system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n   - Avoid references to `$context`, `$output`, or other system nodes.  \n\n6. **Completeness**  \n   - Include only explicitly confirmed milestones such as troubleshooting steps, actions taken, issue resolution, or pending follow-ups.  \n   - Do not infer or assume resolution unless clearly stated.  \n\n7. **Format**  \n   - Output must be **a single paragraph** with no bullets, lists, or subheadings.  \n\n8. **Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details**\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `ProblemDescription` + relevant `MessageContent` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `ProblemDescription`, and all usable `MessageContent` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n1. **Precision**  \n   - Distinguish clearly between **Employee’s issue or feedback**, **IT Support’s actions or responses**, and **system notes**.  \n   - Use clear, specific verbs like *investigated, verified, provided, resolved, escalated, confirmed,* etc.  \n   - Avoid vague language such as “checked,” “worked on,” or “handled.”  \n\n2. **No Assumptions**  \n   - Do not assume the issue is resolved or closed unless explicitly confirmed.  \n   - Do not fabricate missing context or infer actions.  \n\n3. **Chronological Coherence**  \n   - Ensure the narrative reads smoothly and naturally from the initial Employee report to the last recorded update or confirmation.  \n\n4. **Conciseness and Completeness**  \n   - Merge repetitive exchanges while preserving meaning.  \n   - Capture all key IT Support actions, Employee confirmations, and final status within the 1000-character limit.  \n\n\n### Example Summary  \n\n> The Employee reported being unable to access the company VPN. IT Support verified credentials, confirmed the issue was due to an expired token, and guided the Employee to reset it through the authentication portal. After resetting, the Employee confirmed successful login. IT Support validated access logs, ensured network connectivity, and closed the request after confirmation that no further issues were encountered.\n\n---\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n### Language Validation\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first."
            },
            {
              "id": "1760437924593_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
