          "code": "ISRSOLUTIONSUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760437936131",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760437936132_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data\n- **Title**: \n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.Title}}`\n\n- **ProblemDescription**: \n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ProblemDescription}}`\n\n- **ResolveDescription**: \n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ResolveDescription}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES.$output.items}}`\n\nEach message includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` (ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY / ORA_SVC_RESPONSE / ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE)  \n\nUse these inputs to **reconstruct the conversation flow**:  \n- Sort `Messages` in ascending order of `CreationDate`.  \n- Interpret `MessageTypeCd`:  \n  - **ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY** → Customer-reported issue or feedback  \n  - **ORA_SVC_RESPONSE** → IT Support responses\n  - **ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE** → Internal-only notes or system actions (include only if directly relevant)  \n\n---\n\n# Instructions  \nReview the above `Input Data` and write a **detailed yet concise paragraph** summarizing the **solution provided by IT Support to the Employee**. Focus on the **key steps IT Support took to resolve the issue**, Employee confirmations or responses, and explicitly state whether the issue is **closed, remains open, or if any new issues were created**. The summary must be a **single, continuous paragraph**.\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n---\n\n### Mandatory Guidelines  \n\n1. **Scope and Focus**  \n   - Describe only facts present in the record: IT Support solution steps, Employee confirmations or responses, outcomes, closure status, and any newly created issues.  \n\n2. **Role Clarity**  \n   - Refer only to “IT Support” and “Employee.” Do not use names, titles, or other roles.  \n\n3. **Chronological Order**  \n   - Reorder messages based on `CreationDate` to ensure a clear timeline.  \n   - If timestamps are inconsistent, infer logical order (issue → investigation → solution → confirmation).  \n\n4. **Language**  \n   - Use precise, neutral, professional language.  \n   - Avoid speculation, assumptions, or informal phrasing.  \n\n5. **Data Discipline**  \n   - Do not include message type codes or system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n\n6. **Completeness**  \n   - Include only explicitly recorded solution steps, confirmations, and final status.  \n   - Do not infer resolution unless clearly stated.  \n\n7. **Format**  \n   - Output must be **one paragraph**, with no bullets, headings, or sublists.  \n\n8. **Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details**\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `ProblemDescription` + `ResolveDescription` + `MessageContent` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `ProblemDescription`, `ResolveDescription` and all usable `MessageContent` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n1. **Precision**  \n   - Clearly distinguish between **Employee issue**, **IT Support solution steps**, and any **system notes**.  \n   - Use specific verbs like *investigated, resolved, provided, escalated, verified, confirmed*.  \n\n2. **No Assumptions**  \n   - Do not assume closure, resolution, or next steps unless explicitly confirmed.  \n   - Do not fabricate missing details.  \n\n3. **Chronological Coherence**  \n   - Ensure the narrative reads smoothly from IT Support actions to Employee confirmation.  \n\n4. **Conciseness and Completeness**  \n   - Merge repetitive exchanges logically while preserving all key solution steps, confirmations, and final status within 1000 characters.  \n\n\n### Example Summary  \n\n> IT Support identified the cause of the Employee’s VPN connectivity issue as an expired authentication token. They guided the Employee through a reset process and verified successful login. The Employee confirmed access was restored, and IT Support validated system logs. No further issues were reported, and the request was marked as closed.\n\n---\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n### Language Validation\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first."
            },
